---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { DOCS, SITE } from "~/content/site";
---
<Base>
  <section class="rdx-hero rdx-shell" id="brief">
    <div class="rdx-hero-copy">
      <div class="rdx-eyebrow">SELF-HOSTED // LOCAL-FIRST // APACHE-2.0</div>
      <h1>Redact<br />before you<br /><span class="rdx-redact-word">prompt</span>.</h1>
      <p class="rdx-lead">Redax is a local-first PII redaction boundary. Sensitive identifiers are detected and transformed before your application calls an LLM — while you keep control of the host, model files, network, and retention.</p>
      <div class="rdx-actions"><a class="rdx-button rdx-button-primary" href="#demo">Open the live demo <span>↘</span></a><a class="rdx-button" href={DOCS.api}>Read the docs <span>↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="rdx-microfacts"><span>NO HOSTED INFERENCE</span><span>CPU-FRIENDLY PATH</span><span>CONTROL EGRESS</span></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="rdx-file" aria-label="Illustrative redaction case file">
      <div class="rdx-file-tab">CASE FILE // RDX-001</div>
      <div class="rdx-file-head"><h2>Transmission intercept<br />Pre-model boundary</h2><div>DATE 2026.09.30<br />STATUS SAFE TO FORWARD</div></div>
      <p class="rdx-doc-copy">Subject identifies as <span class="rdx-bar">Jordan Reyes</span> from <span class="rdx-bar">Stripe</span>.<br />Contact channel: <span class="rdx-bar">jordan@stripe.com</span>.<br />Voice endpoint: <span class="rdx-bar">+1 (415) 555-2671</span>.</p>
      <pre class="rdx-json">&#123;
  "text": "Hi, I'm [PERSON_0000] from [ORG_0000].
  Reach me at [EMAIL_0000] or [PHONE_E164_0000].",
  "spans": 4,
  "boundary": "local"
&#125;</pre>
      <div class="rdx-classified">SANITIZED</div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="rdx-section" id="product"><div class="rdx-shell rdx-section-grid"><div class="rdx-section-label">FILE 01 / PRODUCT DOCTRINE</div><div><h2>Privacy is the architecture.<br /><span class="rdx-redact-word">Not a feature flag.</span></h2><p class="rdx-sub">Treat the redaction layer like a controlled checkpoint. Raw values enter once, transformed text leaves, and operational metadata remains inspectable.</p><div class="rdx-cards">
    <article><div class="rdx-card-num">01 / DETERMINISM</div><h3>Predictable replacements</h3><p>Structured rules and typed placeholders make the transformation easy to inspect and test.</p></article>
    <article><div class="rdx-card-num">02 / BOUNDARY</div><h3>Local by default</h3><p>Run the service beside your application and keep inference and egress under your control.</p></article>
    <article><div class="rdx-card-num">03 / INTEGRATION</div><h3>One checkpoint</h3><p>Put the redaction call immediately before your existing model request instead of replacing the whole stack.</p></article>
    <article><div class="rdx-card-num">04 / AUDIT</div><h3>Evidence, not exposure</h3><p>Record counts, types, timing, and request metadata without writing original sensitive values into the audit event.</p></article>
  </div></div></div></section>

  <section class="rdx-section" id="demo"><div class="rdx-shell rdx-section-grid"><div class="rdx-section-label">FILE 02 / LIVE DEMONSTRATION</div><div><h2>Type a sentence.<br />Watch the PII disappear.</h2><p class="rdx-sub">This browser-side demonstration uses the structured regex path. It makes no request and does not run the optional server-side model.</p><div class="rdx-demo"><div class="rdx-panel"><div class="rdx-panel-head"><span>RAW INPUT</span><span id="rdx-count">0 CHARS</span></div><textarea id="rdx-raw" spellcheck="false">Email me at alice@example.com or call +1-415-555-2671. My card is 4111 1111 1111 1111.</textarea><div class="rdx-status"><span>BOUNDARY: LOCAL BROWSER</span><span>INPUT // UNCLASSIFIED</span></div></div><div class="rdx-panel rdx-panel-dark"><div class="rdx-panel-head"><span>SAFE PREVIEW</span><span id="rdx-span-count">0 SPANS</span></div><div id="rdx-safe"></div><div class="rdx-status"><span>REPLACEMENT: [TYPE_NNNN]</span><span>OUTPUT // SANITIZED</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="rdx-section" id="pipeline"><div class="rdx-shell rdx-section-grid"><div class="rdx-section-label">FILE 03 / REQUEST LIFECYCLE</div><div><h2>One request.<br />Five controlled stages.</h2><div class="rdx-pipeline">
    <div><b>01</b><section><h3>Regex safety net</h3><p>Catch structured identifiers such as email, phone, IP, card, URL, SSN and IBAN.</p></section><span>stage_01 → detect</span></div>
    <div><b>02</b><section><h3>Contextual entity model</h3><p>Optionally identify people, organisations, and contextual entities using the local model path.</p></section><span>stage_02 → classify</span></div>
    <div><b>03</b><section><h3>Consensus fusion</h3><p>Merge detector spans, resolve overlap, and preserve the strongest label.</p></section><span>stage_03 → resolve</span></div>
    <div><b>04</b><section><h3>Replacement</h3><p>Transform sensitive values into deterministic typed placeholders before the downstream model sees them.</p></section><span>stage_04 → redact</span></div>
    <div><b>05</b><section><h3>Audit boundary</h3><p>Retain operational evidence while keeping original values out of the audit event.</p></section><span>stage_05 ● logged</span></div>
  </div></div></div></section>

  <section class="rdx-section rdx-start" id="start"><div class="rdx-shell rdx-start-inner"><div class="rdx-eyebrow">END OF FILE // CONTINUE LOCALLY</div><h2>Put a safe boundary<br />in front of your model.</h2><p>Run Redax with Docker Compose, send one request, and inspect the transformed output before connecting your existing LLM workflow.</p><div class="rdx-actions"><a class="rdx-button rdx-button-primary" href={DOCS.deployment}>Deployment guide <span>↗</span></a><a class="rdx-button" href={SITE.repo}>View the source <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Base>

<script>
  const raw = document.getElementById("rdx-raw") as HTMLTextAreaElement | null;
  const safe = document.getElementById("rdx-safe");
  const count = document.getElementById("rdx-count");
  const spanCount = document.getElementById("rdx-span-count");
  function escapeHtml(value: string) { return value.replace(/[&<>"']/g, (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;", "'": "&#39;" })[c] ?? c); }
  function render() {
    if (!raw || !safe) return;
    let text = escapeHtml(raw.value); let n = 0;
    for (const [type, pattern] of [["CREDIT_CARD", /\b(?:\d[ -]*?){13,19}\b/g], ["EMAIL", /\b[A-Z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Z0-9.-]+\.[A-Z]{2,}\b/gi], ["PHONE_E164", /(?:\+\d{1,3}[-.\s]?)?(?:\(?\d{3}\)?[-.\s]?)\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{4}\b/g]] as const) text = text.replace(pattern, () => `<span class="rdx-token">[${type}_${String(n++).padStart(4, "0")}]</span>`);
    if (count) count.textContent = `${raw.value.length} CHARS`;
    if (spanCount) spanCount.textContent = `${n} SPAN${n === 1 ? "" : "S"}`;
    safe.innerHTML = text || '<span class="rdx-empty">No input.</span>';
  }
  raw?.addEventListener("input", render); render();
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".rdx-bar").forEach((bar) => bar.addEventListener("click", () => bar.classList.toggle("is-revealed")));
</script>
